        "original_id": "b420a10e-7bfa-53c6-8f69-ba5293c339a3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Only the Brave (2006 film)\n- Organizations: 100th Infantry Battalion, 442nd Regimental Combat Team, 442nd Infantry Regiment (United States)\n- Concepts: Nisei, World War II, segregated military units\n- Places: Europe, Italy, southern France, Germany\n\nFacts:\n- Only the Brave is a 2006 independent film about the 100th Infantry Battalion and the 442nd Regimental Combat Team during World War II.\n- The 100th Infantry Battalion and the 442nd Regimental Combat Team were a segregated World War II fighting unit primarily composed of Nisei Japanese Americans.\n- For its size and length of service, the 100th Infantry Battalion and the 442nd Regimental Combat Team became the most decorated unit in U.S. military history.\n- Beginning in 1944, the 442nd Infantry Regiment fought primarily in Europe during World War II.\n- The 442nd Infantry Regiment fought in Italy, southern France, and Germany.",
